title: CatRecurringTreeDay2
position: 647,285
---
<<start_voice_blip Cat>>
<<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
    <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
<<else>>
    <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
<<endif>>
Gnarp: What you want talk? You choose.
    -> How did you learn those words? <<if $day2AskedCatQ1 == false>>
        <<set $day2AskedCatQ1 = true>>
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        Gnarp: I listen. I repeat. I break sound into parts. Your ship leak many tiny noise: logs, error words, old training tapes.
        Gnarp: I practice alone. I want be understood, not just... heard.
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        Gnarp: First time I talk, I was new. Now I more... independent.
        Gnarp: I can stay on frequency longer. I can keep my fear quiet.
            -> That's terrifying.
                <<positive_indicator Cat>>
                <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
                <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
                Gnarp: It is. But you still here. I still here. That matter.
            -> Oh, those aren't bad. We have those too.
                <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
                <<negative_indicator Cat>>
                <<set $catDislikesYou += 1>>
                Gnarp: You say that like pain is contest. Not kind.
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        Gnarp: You sleep many day. I thought you gone. I hate that thought.
        Gnarp: Then you move again. I send: TEST. HELLO. TALK.
    -> What do you want from me? <<if $day2AskedCatQ2 == false>>
        <<set $day2AskedCatQ2 = true>>
        <<show_character Cat Thinking right>>
        Gnarp: Want? I want... practice being person.
        Gnarp: Where I from, I was small. Two orbit old. People decide everything for me.
        Gnarp: Out here I decide. It is scary.
            -> My mission decides everything too.
                <<positive_indicator Cat>>
                <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
                <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
                Gnarp: Yes. You speak like manual. But you feel like living thing.
                Gnarp: You can be both. I think.
            -> That's not how humans work.
                <<show_character Cat Angry right>>
                Gnarp: You make rule sound like cage. Maybe it is cage.
                <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
                <<negative_indicator Cat>>
                <<set $catDislikesYou += 1>>
    -> What do you do out there, like, day to day? <<if $knowCatJob == false>>
        <<set $knowCatJob = true>>
        <<positive_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
        <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
        Gnarp: I map safe paths. I watch for danger. I fix small things before they become big things.
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        Gnarp: I used to do it because others told me. Now I do it because I choose.
        Gnarp: Independence feel like stepping off ledge and finding air holds you.
    -> Do you have a family? <<if $day2AskedCatQ5 == false>>
        <<set $day2AskedCatQ5 = true>>
        <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
        Gnarp: I have family. I miss them. I worry I left them with too much.
            -> That must be hard.
                <<positive_indicator Cat>>
                <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
                <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
                Gnarp: Yes. But I still breathe. Still do job. That what they taught me: keep going.
            -> Why don't you bring them here?
                <<negative_indicator Cat>>
                <<set $catDislikesYou += 1>>
                <<show_character Cat Angry right>>
                Gnarp: Not that simple. Space hurt people. It hurt you too.
        <<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
            <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
            <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
            Gnarp's voice dips. The translator hesitates like it doesn't want to be responsible for the meaning.
                -> You seemed a little sad just now. Is everything okay?
                    <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
                    Gnarp: I fine. Just... remembering.
                    <<positive_indicator Cat>>
                    <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
                    Gnarp: I lost sibling. Sudden. I still talk to them in my head like they answer.
                    <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
                    Gnarp: Talking to you help. You make space less sharp.
                -> Change the subject.
                    <<jump CatRecurringTreeDay2>>
        <<else>>
            <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
            <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
            Gnarp goes quiet. The silhouette holds still.
                -> ...
                    <<jump CatRecurringTreeDay2>>
        <<endif>>
    -> What do you do for fun? <<if $knowCatPasttime == false>>
        <<set $knowCatPasttime = true>>
        Gnarp: Fun... I watch old broadcasts. I repeat songs. I try jokes. Most jokes fail.
        <<if $catLikesYou >= $catDislikesYou>>
            <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
        <<else>>
            <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        <<endif>>
        Gnarp: I like puzzle. I like pattern. Pattern make world feel less random.
    -> Tell Gnarp something you don't put in reports. <<if $day2AskedCatQ4 == false && $catLikesYou >= $catDislikesYou>>
        <<set $day2AskedCatQ4 = true>>
        <<positive_indicator Cat>>
        <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        I swallow, feeling ridiculous. There's a version of me that only knows how to speak in diagnostics.
        But another version of me is sitting here, alive, with a secret vibrating in my teeth.
        You: I... act confident on paper. In real life I'm scared all the time.
        You: I trained myself to sound like a machine so nobody could hear how lonely I am.
        <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
        Gnarp: I understand this.
        Gnarp: I learn your words. You learn your feelings. We both translate.
        Gnarp: Emotional bilingual.
    -> Do you want to play a game? <<if $day2AskedCatQ3 == false && $knowCatPasttime == true && $catLikesYou >= $catDislikesYou>>
        <<set $day2AskedCatQ3 = true>>
        <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
        Gnarp: Game? Yes. Small safe thing.
        <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
        I let Gnarp beam a simple puzzle to my device: shapes, colors, repeating sequences.
        It shouldn't feel intimate.
        It does anyway.
        <<show_character Cat Sad right>>
        Gnarp falters on patterns that should be easy, like the translator is eating pieces of the rules.
            -> (win at the game)
                <<positive_indicator Cat>>
                <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
                <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
                <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
                Gnarp: You good. Teach me? I want learn from you.
            -> (purposefully lose the game)
                <<show_character Cat Happy2 right>>
                <<positive_indicator Cat>>
                <<set $catLikesYou += 1>>
                <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
                Gnarp: I win! I win!
                Gnarp: Maybe someday I teach you. I practice a lot.
    -> (don't ask any more questions)
        <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<if $posSelfPerception > $negSelfPerception>>
            I decide to end the conversation for now. It's been a while since I've talked with somebody new, but I feel more confident in myself.
        <<else>>
            I feel my social battery start to drain, so I decide to end the conversation for now.
        <<endif>>
        <<start_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<if $catLikesYou > $catDislikesYou>>
            <<show_character Cat Happy right>>
            Gnarp: Already? I was... good. This was good.
            Gnarp: But okay. If you need stop, I understand.
            Gnarp: I will leave now. For now.
        <<else>>
            <<show_character Cat Neutral right>>
            Gnarp: Okay. I go.
        <<endif>>
        <<stop_voice_blip Cat>>
        <<jump AfterGnarpLeavesDay2>>
<<jump CatRecurringTreeDay2>>
===

title: AfterGnarpLeavesDay2
position: 915,224
---
<<hide_all_characters>>
<<play_sound Glitch 0.25>>
The silhouette shudders, then collapses back into static.
<<hide MonitorSilhouette>>
<<show MonitorOn>>
Silence rushes in like a pressure change.
My reflection looks wrong on the dark glass, like someone who knows something they shouldn't.
And now comes the part I'm trained for.
The part with procedures and consequences.
HQ's reminder sits in my inbox, timestamped weeks ago, delivered while I was asleep:
"Remember your duty to report accurately. Your observations are crucial for our understanding and eradication of foreign threats."
Do I report that an alien made contact again, stronger this time, more coherent, more <i>real</i>?
    -> (report Gnarp)
        <<jump WriteReportDay2_Report>>
    -> (do not report)
        <<jump WriteReportDay2_DontReport>>
===

