title: DreamCollegeDay2
position: 915,500
---
<<hide_all_objects>>
<<hide_all_ui_objects>>
<<show Stars>>
<<show Sitting>>
The dream doesn't start in space.
It starts under fluorescent bulbs, with my hands wrapped around cheap coffee and a lab key I wasn't supposed to have.
College was a maze of open doors I couldn't make myself walk through.
Everyone else had study groups, late nights that sounded like laughter, futures that assumed they belonged.
I had silence, and the stubborn thought that if I could become an astronaut, maybe distance would finally feel like relief instead of failure.
I remember the day the decision hardened into something real:
the career counselor's smile that didn't reach her eyes,
the scholarship email I couldn't bring myself to answer,
the long walk back to my dorm where I realized I was already living like I was in orbit: present, but untouchable.
And then the application, the tests, the training.
The way isolation became a skill I could list on a form.
The way I learned to speak in numbers and checklists so nobody could hear the shaking underneath.
In the dream, the stars are there too, just out of reach through a window that doesn't open.
    -> (hold onto the ambition)
        <<set $posSelfPerception += 1>>
        I remember why I wanted this. Not the prestige. The quiet. The distance. The proof that I could endure.
    -> (feel the loneliness)
        <<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
        I remember how easy it was to disappear in a crowd, and how I kept choosing that over being seen.
The dream tilts from college hallway to spacecraft corridor, as if my brain is admitting the truth.
I didn't just get launched into space.
I practiced for it for years.
<<fade_transition 3>>
<<wait 2>>
<<jump StartDay3>>
===

title: KeptUnderWrapsDay2
position: 83,279
---
<<hide_all_ui_objects>>
I sit back from the keyboard, report transmitted, hands still trembling.
<<set $negSelfPerception += 1>>
I did what I'm trained to do. I kept the machine running.
I also did something I'm not trained for at all: I kept a secret that has a pulse.
The same three robotic words keep replaying behind my eyes.
TEST. HELLO. TALK.
I shut the screen down before I can change my mind.
<<jump EndDay2>>
===

